From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 02:37:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86/intel/pmc: Show substate requirements on Tiger
 Lake and Alder Lake-L

tgl_l_pmc_dev and tgl_pmc_dev read the low power mode requirement
registers through the ACPI _DSM (pmc_core_get_tgl_lpm_reqs()), so
substate_requirements is created, but neither sets sub_req_show. The
file is created with NULL fops and reads back empty.

Use pmc_core_substate_req_regs_fops, the show function for the
mode x map layout that the _DSM returns.

Tested on a Surface Pro 9 (i5-1235U, INTEL_ALDERLAKE_L): the file
lists the S0i2.0/S0i3.0 requirements with latched and live status.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/platform/x86/intel/pmc/tgl.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/intel/pmc/tgl.c b/drivers/platform/x86/intel/pmc/tgl.c
index fc5b4cacc..2f91f439f 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/intel/pmc/tgl.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/intel/pmc/tgl.c
@@ -302,6 +302,7 @@ struct pmc_dev_info tgl_l_pmc_dev = {
 	.suspend = cnl_suspend,
 	.resume = cnl_resume,
 	.init = tgl_core_init,
+	.sub_req_show = &pmc_core_substate_req_regs_fops,
 };
 
 struct pmc_dev_info tgl_pmc_dev = {
@@ -309,4 +310,5 @@ struct pmc_dev_info tgl_pmc_dev = {
 	.suspend = cnl_suspend,
 	.resume = cnl_resume,
 	.init = tgl_core_init,
+	.sub_req_show = &pmc_core_substate_req_regs_fops,
 };
